  nonce: '0424'  # 0424
  message: "DONE in PR #2021 (merged; dev 21f8147afa). Cause confirmed in code: js_ts Case 2 (namespace / require-object member call) consulted _disambiguate_by_import -- which resolves a relative specifier to its file over the list-valued symbols_by_name -- only for BARE specifiers, so a relative one fell to the name-keyed global table holding the same-named function enumerated LAST. Fix: relative specifiers take that route too; no candidate in the named file falls through unchanged. BEHAVIOURAL EVIDENCE on merged dev, cold caches: (1) ext4, the re-check's own driver jomik_member_recheck_11022026/scratch_C/povub_drive.py (wrong dir created first, 8 name pairs, both enumeration orders occur): 8/8 CORRECT (the 11-02 re-check: 4/8 wrong); (2) tmpfs, a_early/z_late created in both orders: a_early both times (dev before: a_early / z_late). Production-path tests: test_js_ts.py TestNamespaceImports, test_namespace_import_disambiguates_same_name_functions and a new test_relative_require_object_disambiguates_same_name_functions, each parametrized over creation order; the z_late-first cases go red with the fix reverted. A/B (pre-registered, lab ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/lwr_11022026/): express, jotai 0 moved; knex 2 moved, 0 lost (Knex.js ColumnBuilder.extend / TableBuilder.extend from viewbuilder.js's extend to the columnbuilder.js / tablebuilder.js that Knex.js:10-11 require). Not asserted: other name-keyed tables in js_ts (the general last-write-wins claim); the relative-specifier route does not resolve a directory index (./dir -> dir/index.js), which falls back as before."  # 0424
